      "output": "At its most fundamental level, **water** is a chemical compound and one of the most abundant and essential substances on Earth. \n\nHere is a breakdown of what water is, looking at it through different lenses:\n\n### 1. The Chemical View\nChemically, water is represented by the formula **$\\text{H}_2\\text{O}$**. This means every single molecule of water is made up of:\n*   **Two hydrogen atoms**\n*   **One oxygen atom**\nThese atoms are bonded together by covalent bonds. Water molecules are also \"polar,\" meaning the oxygen side has a slight negative charge and the hydrogen side has a slight positive charge. This polarity is why water molecules stick to each other (hydrogen bonding), giving water its unique properties, like surface tension and the ability to dissolve many substances.\n\n### 2. The Physical View\nWater is famous for being the only natural substance on Earth that exists abundantly in three distinct states of matter within Earth's normal temperature range:\n*   **Liquid:** The standard, free-flowing water we drink, swim in, and find in oceans and rivers.\n*   **Solid (Ice):** Frozen water, which forms glaciers, snow, and ice cubes. Uniquely, solid water is *less dense* than liquid water, which is why ice floats.\n*   **Gas (Vapor/Steam):** Invisible water vapor in the air, clouds, and steam.\n\nWater is odorless, tasteless, and transparent in thin layers, though it has a slight blue tint in thick volumes due to the absorption of red light.\n\n### 3. The Ecological and Geological View\nWater covers about **71% of the Earth's surface**, mostly in oceans and seas (which hold about 96.5% of all Earth's water). The rest is found in polar ice caps, underground aquifers, lakes, rivers, and the atmosphere. \n\nWater is constantly moving through the **water cycle** (evaporation, condensation, precipitation, and collection), cycling endlessly between the Earth and the sky.\n\n### 4. The Biological View\nWater is the **foundation of life** as we know it. \n*   The human body is made up of about 60% water.\n*   Cells are mostly water; it acts as the medium inside which all the chemical reactions of life take place.\n*   It regulates body temperature, transports nutrients, and flushes out"
